'''THE SLOTH''' (ナマルケモルル ''Namarukemoruru'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = THE SLOTH
|image = E 039.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Salty is Seawater|Sub-chapter 4 - Salty is Seawater]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Fleming Seaway|Sub-chapter 15 - Fleming Seaway]]
|money drop = 2,000¢ - 7,900¢
}}

==Enemy==
THE SLOTH is one of the slowest [[Enemy Units]] in both speed and attack rate, but can inflict upwards of 8,000 damage on all [[Cat Units]] within 450 range, the same as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. The result is essentially an upgraded Traitless version of [[The Face]].

He can stall your Cats for a remarkably long time, making him extremely deadly, especially when used as support instead of the main threat in stages like [[Pitfall Zone]], [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on W-Cyclone]]/[[Wrath of W-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of W-Cyclone]] and [[Honey Trap (Deadly)|Honey Trap]]/[[Honey Drip (Deadly)|Honey Drip]], where he easily wipes out your Cats while being protected by either peon spam or other powerful enemies, like [[Director Kurosawah]], [[White Cyclone]] and [[Queen B]], respectively.

In later stages, however, THE SLOTH usually just becomes a wall with high health that doesn't attack often enough to be a major threat since his very long time between attacks makes him easy to stall, and would usually leave many opportunities to slip in hits, eventually defeating him regardless of his strength magnification.

==Strategy==
THE SLOTH is usually being defended by peons in the stages that he appears in. As such, a good strategy is to lure him as close to the [[Cat Base]] as possible, delaying support from other enemies. [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] can then be used to deal heavy damage, while usually being able to survive at least one attack.

Do note that while THE SLOTH can easily stall your Cats, your Cats can also stall him, using his advantage to yours. When there is little to no support such as in his [[Salty is Seawater|debut stage]], simply throwing in periodic [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cats]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cats]] can help stall him while you build up cash for your onslaught.

Some units, such as [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]], can outrange THE SLOTH directly and chip away at him while evading his attacks. [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units can abuse lower-ranged enemies as stepping stones to snipe him. After completing all 3 chapters of [[Into the Future]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used to deal massive amounts of damage during THE SLOTH's long attack interval, but be sure to bait an attack from him before sending him out. This strategy is less consistent later in the game without using CC units to paralyze him, as the extreme stat magnifications allow him to easily survive Bahamut's attacks long enough to retaliate, dealing enough damage to instantly kill Bahamut.

You can also push THE SLOTH with [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Lone Cat and Kitten]] quite easily if THE SLOTH isn't defended by peons or if he isn't the boss. With a combination of Freeze and Knockback against Traitless, THE SLOTH will barely even move, as his low speed makes it difficult for him to recover ground.

