==Trivia==
*THE SLOTH's Japanese name, Namarukemoruru (ナマルケモルル), may be a combination of 鈍る ''namaru'' (to decline in ability, become less capable, or lose one's edge), 怠ける ''namakeru'' (to slack off or laze around) and 樹懶 ''namakemono'' (sloth).
*Since [[Elder Sloth]]'s Japanese name, description and design reference the [[wikia:ghibli:River Spirit|River Spirit]] from the Studio Ghibli movie ''[[wikipedia:Spirited Away|Spirited Away]]'', THE SLOTH's design may have been inspired by [[wikia:ghibli:No-Face|No-Face]] from the same movie.
*The phrase 最強の猛獣 ''saikyō no mōjū'' ("the strongest fierce beast") in THE SLOTH's Japanese description is also used in [[THE FOLIVOREAN]]'s Japanese description and [[The Strongest Behemoth]]'s Japanese name.
*He is Elder Sloth's grandson.

